          <div class="stat-label">Documentation Files</div>
        </div>
        <div class="stat">
          <div class="stat-value">5/day</div>
          <div class="stat-label">Generation Rate</div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <section class="why-section">
        <h2>Why CLI > MCP?</h2>
        <div class="why-grid">
          <div class="why-item">
            <h3>⚡ Faster</h3>
            <p>Direct API calls. No server overhead. No abstraction layers. Just raw performance.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <h3>💰 Cheaper</h3>
            <p>No server costs. No token usage for every operation. Run locally, pay nothing.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <h3>🎯 Simpler</h3>
            <p>Standard Unix philosophy. Pipe, redirect, compose. No new abstractions to learn.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <h3>🔒 Deterministic</h3>
            <p>Same input, same output. Every time. No AI unpredictability in your workflows.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <h3>🛠️ Debuggable</h3>
            <p>See exactly what's happening. Full control. No black box between you and the API.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="why-item">
            <h3>📦 Portable</h3>
            <p>Works anywhere Node.js runs. No special runtime. No server dependencies.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

